{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In the third month.</b> That is the month of Sivan. <b>On this day</b> — it was Rosh Chodesh. Which day is called חדש? You must say: this is Rosh Chodesh, as it is written (I Samuel 20:24): ״ויהי החדש וישב המלך אל הלחם לאכול״, and it is written (ibid.): ״ויהי ממחרת החדש השני ויפקד מקום דוד״. And Scripture teaches you that there were two days of Rosh Chodesh, and this is what is written (ibid.): ״ויאמר שאול אל יהונתן בנו מדוע לא בא בן ישי גם תמול גם היום אל הלחם״. And so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: <b>on this day</b> — it was Rosh Chodesh. It is written here ״ביום הזה״, and it is written there (Exodus 12:2): ״החדש הזה לכם״." "<b>They came into the wilderness of Sinai.</b> That is Chorev, concerning which it is written (Exodus 3:1): ״ויבא אל הר האלהים חורבה״, and concerning it was said (ibid. v. 12): ״בהוציאך את העם ממצרים תעבדון את האלהים על ההר הזה״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Citation 'שמואל א כ׳:כ״ד' given without book name in source; resolved as I Samuel 20:24 from context. The prooftext from ibid. is I Samuel 20:27."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:52.887796489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}